          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+category"} homotopical category
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            equipped with the information that some of its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mi Core
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \supset Core(C)
            = succeed "," do
              %strong simplicial localization
            = succeed "." do
              %strong Dwyer–Kan localization
          %p
            The
            %em simplicial localization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L C
            of a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            realized concretely as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+category"} simplicially enriched category
            which is such that the original category injects into it,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi L
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \hookrightarrow L C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            that is labeled as a weak equivalence becomes an actual equivalence in the sense of morphisms in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L C
            is in some sense universal with this property.
          %p
            Passing to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} homotopy category of an (∞,1)-category
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L C
            then reproduces the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            that can also directly be obtained from
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ho
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Ho_C(a,b) \simeq \Pi_0 (L C(a,b))
          %p
            (where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0
            gives the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+homotopy+group"} 0th simplicial homotopy groupoid
          %p
            If the homotopical structure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            extends to that of a (combinatorial)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category presented by a combinatorial model category
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            See also
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                localization of a simplicial model category
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/localization+of+a+simplicial+model+category"} ?
          %h2#construction Construction
          %p
            See
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localization+of+a+homotopical+category"} simplicial localization of a homotopical category
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#standard_simplicial_localization “Standard” simplicial localization
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Cat
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Grph
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U : \mathbf{Cat} \to \mathbf{Grph}
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            that sends a (small) category to its underlying
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflexive+graph"} reflexive
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph"} graph
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Grph
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : \mathbf{Grph} \to \mathbf{Cat}
            be its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔾
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{G} = (G, \epsilon, \delta)
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Cat}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mo •
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Cat
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Δ
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_\bullet : \mathbf{Cat} \to [\mathbf{\Delta}^{op}, \mathbf{Cat}]
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+objects+in+Cat"} simplicial objects in Cat
            equipped with a canonical augmentation, where
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi n
                    %mi C
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi G
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_n C = G^{n+1} C
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong standard resolution
              of a small category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is defined to be the simplicial category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mo •
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_\bullet C
          %p
            Note that this is also a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+category"} simplicial category
            in the strong sense, i.e.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ob
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mo •
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ob G_\bullet C
            is discrete! Thus we may also regard
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mo •
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_\bullet C
            as an
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution"} resolution
            in the sense that the augmentation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mo •
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon : G_\bullet C \to C
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dwyer-Kan+equivalence"} Dwyer-Kan equivalence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mo •
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_\bullet C (X, Y) \to C (X, Y)
            admits an extra degeneracy and hence a contracting homotopy.)
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong standard simplicial localization
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+category"} relative category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C, W)
              is the simplicial category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\bullet (C, W)
              where
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mi n
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi G
                            %mi n
                          %mi W
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_n (C, W) = G_n C [{G_n W}^{-1}]
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#DwyerKanLocalizations"}> DwyerKanLocalizations, def. 4.1
            ). Again,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mo •
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\bullet C
            is a simplicial category in the strong sense, because
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mo •
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_\bullet C
            is.
          %h3#hammock_localization Hammock localization
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,W)
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y \in C
              any two objects, write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi H
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L^H C(X,Y) \in sSet
            %p
              for the simplicial set defined as follows. For each natural number
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              defined as follows:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  are length-
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  zig-zags of morphisms in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mover
                          %mo ←
                          %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %mi K
                          %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi K
                          %mn 2
                        %mover
                          %mo ←
                          %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %mi K
                          %mn 3
                        %mo →
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        X \stackrel{\simeq}{\leftarrow}
                        K_1 \to K_2 \stackrel{\simeq}{\leftarrow} K_3 \to
                        \\cdots \to Y
                        \\,,
                %p
                  where the left-pointing morphisms are to be in
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              %li
                %p
                  its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                  are “natural transformations” between such objects, fixing the endpoints:
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
