                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        \&amp;&amp; K_1 &amp;\to&amp; K_2 &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\leftarrow}&amp;
                        \\cdots
                        \\\
                        \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\simeq}}\swarrow
                        \&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \searrow^{}
                        \\\
                        X
                        \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\simeq}&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\simeq}&amp; \cdots&amp;&amp;  &amp;&amp; Y
                        \\\
                        \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{\simeq}}\nwarrow
                        \&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \nearrow^{}
                        \\\
                        \&amp;&amp; L_1 &amp;\to&amp; L_2 &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\leftarrow}&amp;
                        \\cdots
                        }
                        \\;
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi H
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^H C(X,Y)
              is obtained by
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  taking the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerves"} nerves
                  of these categories over all
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %li
                %p
                  quotienting by the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
                  generated by inserting or removing identity morphisms and composing composable morphisms.
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y,Z
              three objects, there is an evident compositing morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi H
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi H
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi H
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L^H C(X,Y) \times L^H C(Y,Z) \to L^H C(X,Z)
            %p given by horizontally concatenating hammock diagrams as above.
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+category"} simplicially enriched category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi H
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^H C
              obtained this way is the
              %strong hammock localization
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,W)
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#DwyerKanCalculating"}> DwyerKanCalculating, def. 2.1
            ).
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#basic_properties Basic properties
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,W)
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi H
                    %mi C
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^H C \in sSet Cat
              for its hammock localization and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C[W^{-1}] \in Cat
              for its ordinary
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi H
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(L^H C) \in Cat
              for the category with the same objects as
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and morphisms between
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              being the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %msup
                        %mi L
                        %mi H
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0 L^H C(X,Y)
            %p
              There is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi H
                    %mi C
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Ho L^H C
                    \\simeq
                    C[W^{-1}]
                    \\,.
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#DwyerKanCalculating"}> DwyerKanCalculating, prop. 3.1
            ).
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              Hammock localization is clearly a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              from the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+categories"} relative categories
              to
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet-enriched+categories"} sSet-enriched categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi RelativeCat
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi L
                          %mi W
                          %mi H
                    %mi SimplicialCategories
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    RelativeCat \overset{L^H_W}{\longrightarrow} SimplicialCategories
            %p
          %p
            See also
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BarwickKan12"} Barwick &amp; Kan 12, Sec. 1.5
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Spitzweck10"} Spitzweck 10, p. 3
          #PrePostCompositionWithWeakEquivalences.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,W)
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi W
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (X \overset{f}{\to} Y) \in W \subset Mor(C)
            %p
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in C
              we have that the concatenation operation on hammocks induce
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalences"} weak homotopy equivalences
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi H
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi H
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f_*
                    \\;\colon\;
                    L^H C(U,X)
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                    L^H C(U,Y)
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi H
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi H
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f^*
                    \\;\colon\;
                    L^H C(Y,U)
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                    L^H C(X, U)
                    \\,.
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#DwyerKanCalculating"}> DwyerKanCalculating, prop. 3.3
            ).
          %h3#simplical_localization_gives_all_categories
            Simplical localization gives all
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Up to Dwyer-Kan equivalence –the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+sSet-categories"} model structure on sSet-categories
              – every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+category"} simplicial category
              is the simplicial localization of a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
            %p
              This is (
              %a{:href => "#DwyerKanEquivalences"}> DwyerKan 87, 2.5
              ).
          %p
            If the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
            in question happens to carry even the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            there exist more refined tools for computing the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom+object"} hom object
            of the simplicial localization. These are described at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categorical+hom-space"} (∞,1)-categorical hom-space
          %h3#equivalences_between_simplicial_localizations Equivalences between simplicial localizations
          #SimplicialLocalizationOfNaturalTransformation.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,W)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C', W')
              be
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+with+weak+equivalences"} categories with weak equivalences
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi H
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi H
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^H C, L^H C' \in sSet Cat
              for the corresponding
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hammock+localizations"} hammock localizations
            %p
              Then for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 2
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_1, F_2 :  C \to C'
              two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+functors"} homotopical functors
              (functors respecting the weak equivalences, i.e.
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi W
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_i(W) \subset W'
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta : F_1 \Rightarrow F_2
            %p
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              with components in the
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W'
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y \in C
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
              between morphisms of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi L
                              %mi H
                            %mi C
                            %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi F
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi F
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi L
                                    %mi H
                                  %msub
                                    %mi F
                                    %mn 1
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi η
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi Y
                                  %msub
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi L
                              %mi H
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi L
                              %mi H
                            %mi C
                            %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi F
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi F
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi L
                                    %mi H
                                  %msub
                                    %mi F
                                    %mn 2
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi η
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi X
                                  %msup
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi L
                              %mi H
                            %mi C
                            %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi F
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi F
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; L^H C'(F_1(X), F_1(Y) )
                    \\\
                    \&amp;
                    {}^{\mathllap{L^H F_1}}\nearrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\searrow^{\mathrlap{\eta(Y)_*}}
                    \\\
                    L^H C(X,Y)
                    \&amp;&amp; \Downarrow &amp;&amp;
                    L^H C'(F_1(X), F_2(Y))
                    \\\
                    \&amp;
                    {}_{\mathllap{L^H F_2}}\searrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\nearrow_{\mathrlap{\eta(X)^*}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; L^H C' (F_2(X), F_2(Y))
                    }
                    \\,.
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#DwyerKanComputations"}> DwyerKanComputations, prop. 3.5
            ).
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i : (C_1, W_1) \hookrightarrow (C_2, W_2)
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                  is homotopy-essentially surjective: for every object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi c
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_2 \in C_2
                  there is an object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi c
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_1 \in C_1
                  and a weak equivalence
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi c
                            %mn 2
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mo ≃
                          %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi c
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_2 \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} i(c_1)
              %li
                %p
                  there is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Q
                        %mo :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi W
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi W
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q : (C_2,W_2) \to (C_1, W_1)
                  and a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi Q
                        %mo ⇒
                        %msub
                          %mi Id
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mn 2
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        i \circ Q  \Rightarrow Id_{C_2}
                        \\,.
            %p
              Then we have an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} equivalence of (∞,1)-categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi H
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi H
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L^H C_1 \simeq L^H C_2
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              We have to check that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+surjective+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} essentially surjective (∞,1)-functor
              and a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} full and faithful (∞,1)-functor
            %p
              The first condition is immediate from the first assumption. The second follows with prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SimplicialLocalizationOfNaturalTransformation"}
              (using prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PrePostCompositionWithWeakEquivalences"}
          %h3#simplicial_localization_of_model_categories Simplicial localization of model categories
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo ∘
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\circ
              for the full
              = succeed "-subcategory" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
            %p
              Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo ∘
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\circ
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi H
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^H C
              are connected by an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} equivalence of (∞,1)-categories
          %p
            This is one of the central statements in (
            %a{:href => "#DwyerKan80FunctionComplexes"}> Dwyer &amp; Kan 80 FuncComp
            ). The weak homotopy equivalence between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo ∘
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\circ(X,Y)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi H
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^H C(X,Y)
            is in corollary 4.7. The equivalence of
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          #QuillenEquivalencesInducingDKEquivalences.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo ⇆
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \leftrightarrows C
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
              induces a Dwyer-Kan-equivalence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi C
                    %mo ↔
                    %mi L
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L C \leftrightarrow L D
              between their
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localizations"} simplicial localizations
          %p
            This is made explicit in
            %a{:href => "#MazelGee15"} Mazel-Gee 15, p. 17
            to follow from
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#DwyerKan80FunctionComplexes"} Dwyer &amp; Kan 80 FuncComp, Prop. 4.4 with 5.4
          %h3#PresentationCSS Presentation in terms of complete Segal spaces
          %p
            Using
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicategories"} quasicategories
            as a model of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} (infinity,1)-categories
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+Segal+spaces"} complete Segal spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+Segal+spaces#RelationToSimplicialLocalization"} complete Segal spaces#RelationToSimplicialLocalization
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localizer"} localizer
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localizing+subcategory"} localizing subcategory
          %h2#References References
          %p The original articles:
          %ul
            %li#DwyerKanLocalizations
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"}> William Dwyer
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Kan"} Daniel Kan
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Simplicial localizations of categories
                %strong 17
                3 (1980), 267-284 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-4049(80)90049-3"}> doi:10.1016/0022-4049(80)90049-3
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#DwyerKanCalculating
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"}> William Dwyer
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Kan"} Daniel Kan
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Calculating simplicial localizations
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-4049(80)90113-9"} doi:10.1016/0022-4049(80)90113-9
            %li#DwyerKan80FunctionComplexes
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"}> William Dwyer
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Kan"} Daniel Kan
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Function complexes in homotopical algebra
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0040-9383(80)90025-7"} doi:10.1016/0040-9383(80)90025-7
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://people.math.rochester.edu/faculty/doug/otherpapers/dwyer-kan-3.pdf"} pdf
            %li#DwyerKanEquivalences
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"}> William Dwyer
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Kan"} Daniel Kan
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Equivalences between homotopy theories of diagrams
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic topology and algebraic K-theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 113
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1515/9781400882113-009"} doi:10.1515/9781400882113-009
          %p and in modernized form:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"}> William Dwyer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philip+Hirschhorn"} Philip Hirschhorn
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Kan"} Daniel Kan
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeff+Smith"} Jeff Smith
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopy+Limit+Functors+on+Model+Categories+and+Homotopical+Categories"} Homotopy Limit Functors on Model Categories and Homotopical Categories
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 113
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/surv-113-s"} ISBN: 978-1-4704-1340-8
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://dodo.pdmi.ras.ru/~topology/books/dhks.pdf"} pdf
          %p Survey:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tim+Porter"}> Tim Porter
                , Section 4.1 of:
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  \-Categories,
                  = succeed "-groupoids," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0401274"}> arXiv:math/0401274
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clark+Barwick"}> Clark Barwick
                , Section 2 of:
                %em On (enriched) Bousfield localization of model categories
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0708.2067"}> arXiv:0708.2067
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Further development:
          %ul
            %li#BarwickKan12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clark+Barwick"}> Clark Barwick
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Kan"} Daniel Kan
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A characterization of simplicial localization functors and a discussion of DK equivalences
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.indag.2011.10.001"} doi:10.1016/j.indag.2011.10.001
            %li#Hinich13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Hinich"}> Vladimir Hinich
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Dwyer-Kan Localization Revisited
                = succeed "," do
